  "final_text": "Both objects now exist in Kibana 9.5.5.\n\n**Data exploration:** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) holds web-server access logs. The useful fields are `clientip`, `response` / `response.keyword` (status codes), `bytes`, `extension.keyword`, `url.keyword`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, and `agent`. I could not run ES|QL or search queries directly, because this Kibana doesn't expose the query endpoints I tried, so I checked the field list and chose the panels from it rather than from the data's actual values.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-d1ed917d Web logs overview`** (id `eff-d1ed917d-web-logs-overview-63918d467541`, last 7 days)\n1. Total requests (metric, count)\n2. Unique client IPs (metric, unique count of `clientip`)\n3. Total bytes transferred (metric, sum of `bytes`)\n4. Requests over time (line, date histogram)\n5. Responses by status code (pie, top 10 `response.keyword`)\n6. Top requested extensions (bar, top 10 `extension.keyword`)\n7. 5xx responses (ES|QL metric: `RLIKE \"5[0-9][0-9]\"` count)\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-d1ed917d 5xx spike`** (id `a87ed4c6-58c8-457a-9f0e-676f6febe689`)\n- Type `.es-query` in ES|QL mode, consumer `stackAlerts`, runs every 1m, enabled, tagged `EFF-d1ed917d`.\n- Query: counts documents in the rule's time window with `response.keyword` matching `5xx`, then `WHERE errors > 10`. Kibana rejected a plain `threshold: [10]` for ES|QL rules, so the threshold lives in the query and the rule's own threshold is `[0]` with `>`.\n- Window is 5 minutes.\n\n**Choices to review:**\n- I enabled the rule. The request said it should check every minute, so I treated that as running. Disable it if you want it created but idle.\n- I used the 5xx match `RLIKE \"5[0-9][0-9]\"` on the string field rather than a numeric range.\n- The rule status is `ok` right after creation. I did not confirm that it evaluates correctly against live data, because I couldn't run the ES|QL query myself.",
